---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const sources = [
  ["Trading fees", "Every trade in the KYP pool (RHEA DCL) pays a fee to a permanent liquidity position the coordinator owns and cannot remove."],
  ["Reserved slots", "Money from reserved slots bought after launch goes into the same split."],
];

const destinations = [
  {
    title: "Holders",
    mark: "Live",
    kind: "live",
    body: "A share goes to holders outside the presale group. Today this is paid to the holders account the launcher names. Paying each holder on-chain is not built yet.",
  },
  {
    title: "Operations (default, capped)",
    mark: "Live",
    kind: "live",
    body: "A set percentage of fees, capped at 30%, is paid to the operations account the launcher names, for running costs such as DexScreener, listings, bots and hosting. Paid straight to that account. Default on a new launch is 0%; an example is 20%.",
  },
  {
    title: "NEAR AI credits",
    mark: "Live",
    kind: "live",
    body: "A set percentage of fees, capped at 20%, is paid to the NEAR AI credits account the launcher names, to buy credits the project uses (for example the Cabal Corner agent and other AI tooling). Default on a new launch is 0%; an example is 10%.",
  },
  {
    title: "Content and creators",
    mark: "Partly live",
    kind: "part",
    body: "The locked presalers' fee share funds quality content. The caballeros agree among themselves on bounties, and can post them on NEARN to bring in artists and creators, who can use the best AI tools or none at all. Cabal Corner already lets the roster vote on bounties and attach a NEARN listing link. After approval, the launcher or the community account can pay the claimant on-chain from the undistributed community fee share.",
  },
  {
    title: "The lock",
    mark: "Live",
    kind: "live",
    body: "A share of fees, taken from the liquidity slice and capped at 20%, can be swapped on the RHEA DCL pool into the project token and added to the permanent lock (an account that does not claim). Default on a new launch is 0%; an example is 10%. Anyone can trigger a buyback once the launcher sets the share. A minimum output protects the swap; failed swaps credit the quote back to the fee pool.",
  },
  {
    title: "Smarter liquidity",
    mark: "Planned",
    kind: "planned",
    body: "Fees fund liquidity in price bands below the current price for support, and around the current price to earn more fees. Today the liquidity share is paid to the liquidity account the launcher names.",
  },
  {
    title: "Partner pools",
    mark: "Planned",
    kind: "planned",
    body: "Fees seed shared pools with other NEAR communities, building friendships and volume together.",
  },
  {
    title: "Bounties and competitions",
    mark: "Live",
    kind: "part",
    body: "Fees fund open NEARN bounties for memes, campaigns, dev work and translations, open to everyone. Cabal Corner already has voted bounties and competitions sized against the community fee share, and a Post on NEARN button plus a place to paste the listing link. After the roster approves a delivery, the launcher (or the community account) records `approve_bounty` on-chain; anyone can then pay the claimant from the community fee share. The launcher can also approve and pay in one wallet transaction.",
  },
];
---
<Base title="The flywheel" active="/flywheel" description="How KYP puts trading fees and reserved-slot proceeds back to work for the project. The on-chain split is live on testnet; the finer destinations are the planned fee design.">
  <section class="hero full-bleed" style="padding-bottom: 20px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div>
        <span class="pill planned">Planned fee design</span>
        <h1>The flywheel</h1>
        <p class="lead">Every trade earns fees, and KYP puts those fees back to work for the project.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fly" style="padding-top: 24px; padding-bottom: 96px">
    <div class="card reveal fly-now">
      <h3>What's live today, and what is planned</h3>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 8px">On testnet, reserved-slot proceeds and any fees sent to the coordinator are split on-chain. The default split is 50% holders, 30% liquidity, 20% community (competitions and bounties). Each launch can also add two capped legs — operations (max 30%) and NEAR AI credits (max 20%) — paid to the accounts the launcher names. Anyone can trigger the payout. After a Corner vote, the launcher or the community account records `approve_bounty` on-chain; anyone can then pay the claimant from the undistributed community fee share. Anyone can call `collect_fees` to claim charged RHEA DCL trading fees from the coordinator-owned permanent LP into the fee pool. The launcher can set a lock buyback share (from the liquidity slice, max 20%); anyone can then swap that quote on the pool into the token for the permanent lock. The remaining destinations below are still planned.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="fly-flow reveal" aria-label="Fee flow: trading fees and reserved slots feed a pool that splits to holders, liquidity and community, then to planned uses">
      <div class="fly-row">
        <div class="fly-box">Trading fees<span>RHEA DCL pool</span></div>
        <div class="fly-box">Reserved slots<span>bought after launch</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="fly-join" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="fly-box fly-pool">Fee pool<span>split on-chain, per launch</span></div>
      <div class="fly-join" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="fly-row fly-three">
        <div class="fly-box on">Holders<span>Live</span></div>
        <div class="fly-box on">Liquidity<span>Live</span></div>
        <div class="fly-box on">Community<span>Live</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="fly-join" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="fly-row fly-plan">
        <div class="fly-box on">Operations<span>Live</span></div>
        <div class="fly-box on">NEAR AI credits<span>Live</span></div>
        <div class="fly-box dim">Content</div>
        <div class="fly-box on">The lock<span>Live</span></div>
        <div class="fly-box dim">Smarter LP</div>
        <div class="fly-box dim">Partner pools</div>
        <div class="fly-box dim">Open bounties</div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>The holders, liquidity, community, operations, NEAR AI credit and lock buyback shares are live. Content, smarter LP, partner pools and open bounties are still partly live or planned.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="head reveal" style="margin-top: 56px; margin-bottom: 24px">
      <h2>Where fees come from</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid g2">
      {sources.map(([t, d]) => (
        <div class="card reveal">
          <h3 style="margin-bottom: 8px">{t}</h3>
          <p class="muted">{d}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="head reveal" style="margin-top: 56px; margin-bottom: 24px">
      <h2>Where fees go</h2>
      <p>Splits are configurable per launch. The live on-chain default is 50% holders, 30% liquidity, 20% community, with operations and NEAR AI credits at 0%. An example is 20% operations and 10% NEAR AI credits, taken from the other slices. Operations are capped at 30%, NEAR AI credits at 20%.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid g2">
      {destinations.map((d) => (
        <div class="card reveal">
          <div class="fly-card-head">
            <h3>{d.title}</h3>
            <span class={`mark ${d.kind}`}>{d.mark}</span>
          </div>
          <p class="muted">{d.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="note reveal" style="margin-top: 28px">NEARN is at <a class="link" href="https://nearn.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">nearn.io</a>. See also <a class="link" href="/how-it-works">How it works</a> and <a class="link" href="/corner">Cabal Corner</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
